<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Better Traders Guild - NPC crib tuck job definition

    BTG_BringBabyToSafety: the caretaker/garrison "put this infant back in a crib" job.
    Runs vanilla's own JobDriver_BringBabyToSafety unchanged; only the carry flags differ.
    Vanilla's BringBabyToSafety keeps the JobDef defaults (dropThingBeforeJob true,
    carryThingAfterJob false), which are fine for a colonist fetching a baby off the floor
    but wrong for BTG's carers, who routinely START the tuck already holding the infant (a
    ferry interrupted by a lord phase change, a bottle-feed's aftermath): starting the
    vanilla job dropped the infant at the carer's feet, the driver's pickup toils lifted it
    again, and any interruption mid-walk dropped it once more - the visible pick/drop/retuck
    churn. With these flags the driver's already-carrying jump is taken directly and an
    interrupted tuck keeps the infant in arms for whichever giver runs next (the tuck's own
    carried branch, or the escape carry).

    A separate JobDef rather than retargeting vanilla's so colony childcare is untouched.
    Used by: JobGiver_BTGTuckBabyInCrib (shelter/stranded caretaker and garrison duties).
  -->

  <JobDef>
    <defName>BTG_BringBabyToSafety</defName>
    <driverClass>JobDriver_BringBabyToSafety</driverClass>
    <reportString>putting TargetA somewhere safe.</reportString>
    <forceCompleteBeforeNextJob>true</forceCompleteBeforeNextJob>
    <dropThingBeforeJob>false</dropThingBeforeJob>
    <carryThingAfterJob>true</carryThingAfterJob>
  </JobDef>

</Defs>
